  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "HAsCWlFcWy0YEEujzLqFlk9IjsM=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:31:37.967Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The correction on Kainos changes the status of a number without changing the number. Framework access had been asserted at 5 with no evidence behind it; verification confirmed 5, backed by 15 lots across 8 Crown Commercial Service frameworks. The digit is identical and its decision value is not.\n\nThat distinction matters for the corpus as a whole. An asserted score and a verified score look the same in a ranking, and the correction log is the only place the difference is recorded. Any downstream use of these scores that reads the columns without the flags will treat guesses and findings as interchangeable.\n\nThe row also carries a tension. Kainos has maximal public-sector framework access, verified, plus a deep proprietary stack \u2014 Workday as Europe's largest boutique partner, Microsoft Solutions Partner, AWS Advanced Consulting and Premier MSP with 500+ certified engineers \u2014 across public, NHS and banking verticals. It nonetheless sits in the do-not-pitch tier, and the flag does not say which input produced that placement; the row is a provisional v2 entry with an OSS-portfolio screen still outstanding.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- Kainos (UK)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> \u26a0 CORRECTION (Framework access evidence): was asserted 5, unevidenced \u2192 now 5 - confirmed on 15 lots across 8 Crown Commercial Service frameworks. DERIVED, NOT SCORED ON v3 \u2014 v2 row rescored mechanically (size + slot-occupancy only). Run the OSS-portfolio screen before acting. v2 verticals: Public, healthcare (NHS), banking",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:31:37.967836Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:31:37.967841Z"
    }
  },
